# project: patient-scheduling-rollout
// New patient-scheduling system rollout across four clinics:
// pilot at the smallest clinic, then the remaining three one at a time.

VAR clinics_live = 0

-> pilot_training

=== pilot_training ===
Train the front-desk staff at the smallest clinic on the new scheduling system.
Done when the pilot clinic's front desk can run the new system unaided.
* [Front-desk staff trained] -> pilot_run

=== pilot_run ===
Run the new system at the pilot clinic for two weeks with the old system as fallback.
Every scheduling incident is logged for the clinical safety officer's review.
+ [Two-week parallel run complete] -> pilot_safety_review

=== pilot_safety_review ===
The clinical safety officer reviews every scheduling incident from the pilot run
before the pilot can be called done. Extending the pilot is her prerogative,
as often as she needs.
+ [Extend the pilot, run again] @human ~loop~ -> pilot_run
+ [All incidents reviewed, pilot is done] @human -> manager_signoff

=== clinic_training ===
Train the front-desk staff at the next remaining clinic, same pattern as the pilot.
+ [Front-desk staff trained] -> clinic_run

=== clinic_run ===
Run the new system at this clinic for one week with the old system as fallback.
Any patient-safety incident anywhere pauses the whole rollout.
+ [Patient-safety incident reported] -> rollout_pause
+ [One-week parallel run complete] -> clinic_safety_review

=== rollout_pause ===
The whole rollout is paused while the clinical safety officer investigates the
patient-safety incident. Nothing proceeds until she clears it.
+ [Safety officer clears the incident, resume] @human ~loop~ -> clinic_run

=== clinic_safety_review ===
The clinical safety officer reviews this clinic's scheduling incidents before
the clinic can be called ready.
+ [Extend this clinic's parallel run] @human ~loop~ -> clinic_run
+ [Incidents reviewed, clinic is ready] @human -> manager_signoff

=== manager_signoff ===
This clinic's practice manager signs off before the clinic goes fully live
and the old-system fallback is removed.
+ [Practice manager signs off, go fully live] @human -> go_live

=== go_live ===
The clinic is fully live on the new scheduling system and the fallback is removed.
~ clinics_live += 1
+ {clinics_live < 4} [Start the next clinic] ~loop~ -> clinic_training
* {clinics_live >= 4} [All four clinics live] -> archive_period

=== archive_period ===
The old system goes read-only and IT keeps a 90-day archive so records
requests can still be served.
* [90-day retention window complete] -> decommission

=== decommission ===
Decommission the old scheduling system entirely.
-> END
